The version script exports the sd-event integration entry points
(sd_bus_{attach,detach,get}_event), but basu ships no sd-event and no
implementation of these three functions exists anywhere in the tree.
GNU ld silently ignores version-script assignments for undefined
symbols; LLD makes them a hard error ("version script assignment of
'global' to symbol ... failed"), so the library does not link on
clang/lld toolchains (Chimera/Astro). Drop the dead exports.

--- a/src/libsystemd/libsystemd.sym
+++ b/src/libsystemd/libsystemd.sym
@@ -72,9 +72,6 @@
         sd_bus_get_current_message;
         sd_bus_get_current_handler;
         sd_bus_get_current_userdata;
-        sd_bus_attach_event;
-        sd_bus_detach_event;
-        sd_bus_get_event;
         sd_bus_add_filter;
         sd_bus_add_match;
         sd_bus_add_object;
